hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21417","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri, saying: Sahl al-Ansari said, and he had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was fifteen years old in his time: Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, narrated to me that the fatwa they used to say, water is from water, was a concession the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted in the beginning of Islam, then he commanded us to wash afterwards."
"21418","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Yunus informed me from al-Zuhri from Sahl ibn Sad al-Ansari, and he had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was fifteen years old, who said: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that the fatwa they used to give in their saying, water is from water, was a concession granted in the beginning of Islam, then we were commanded to wash afterwards."
"21419","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yunus from al-Zuhri from Sahl from Ubayy similar to it. Ibn al-Mubarak said: Mamar informed me with this isnad similar to it."
"21420","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Ibn Shihab said: Sahl ibn Sad said, and he had reached fifteen years when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and he heard from him: Ubayy ibn Kab informed me, and he mentioned similar to it."
"21421","Abu al-Yaman informed us: Shuayb informed us from al-Zuhri, saying: Sahl ibn Sad al-Ansari said, and he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him, and mentioned he was fifteen years old, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that the fatwa they used to give was a concession the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted in the beginning of Islam, then he commanded us to wash afterwards."
"21422","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Rishdin narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Ibn Shihab: one whom I approve narrated to me from Sahl ibn Sad that Ubayy narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it a concession for the believers due to the scarcity of their garments, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it afterwards, meaning their saying, water is from water."
"21423","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us: al-Aslami, meaning Abdullah ibn Amir, narrated to me from Imran ibn Abi Anas from Sahl ibn Sad from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mosque founded upon piety, and he said: It is my mosque."
"21424","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated to us from Imran ibn Abi Anas from Sahl ibn Sad from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mosque founded upon piety is this mosque of mine."
